                    "After a pause came 'O you enveloped one, arise and warn!' (74:1-2). Three years of quiet calling followed: the first believers were Khadijah; Abu Bakr among men; Ali among boys; Zaid. Through Abu Bakr came Uthman, az-Zubayr, Abdur-Rahman ibn Awf, Sa'd, Abu Ubaydah and Talhah — among the ten promised Paradise. Muslims gathered secretly in Dar al-Arqam to learn the Qur'an.",
