                    "Year three: 3,000 Quraysh came for revenge. Fifty archers held the mountain on strict orders. Victory came first; most archers descended for spoils; Khalid — then a pagan — wheeled around the hill. Seventy fell, including Hamzah, master of martyrs, and Mus'ab the standard-bearer. Wounded, tooth broken, the Prophet climbed the rock praying: 'O Allah, forgive my people, they know not.' Revelation taught accountability: victory is tied to discipline, not guaranteed.",
